            "value" : "Your watch\nis ready"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your watch taps a long swell in, then a longer fade out, so you can keep your eyes shut and follow it. Queasy suggests three seconds in and five out when things are mild, and four in and eight out when they are not. Breathing out for longer than you breathe in is the whole technique.\n\nSmall trials of slow diaphragmatic breathing during chemotherapy and after surgery have reported lower nausea scores. They are small, and the reviewers say so." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your watch taps a long swell in, then a longer fade out, so you can keep your eyes shut and follow it. Queasy suggests three seconds in and five out when things are mild, and four in and eight out when they are not. Breathing out for longer than you breathe in is the whole technique.\n\nSmall trials of slow diaphragmatic breathing during chemotherapy and after surgery have reported lower nausea scores. They are small, and the reviewers say so."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your watch taps the rhythm so you can keep your eyes shut: a long tap in, a longer one out. Breathing out for longer than you breathe in is the whole technique." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your watch taps the rhythm so you can keep your eyes shut: a long tap in, a longer one out. Breathing out for longer than you breathe in is the whole technique."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your whole history, and what helps" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
